@title Edge proxy TLS certificate rotation
@subtitle Redwater Media Platform runbook for the 18 edge proxies
@author Platform Security

kpi Rotate at | 30 days or fewer left | CERT_EXPIRY_30D
kpi Edge proxies | 18
kpi Hostnames | 12
kpi Rollback window | 7 days

## When to rotate

Rotate when a certificate has 30 days or fewer left. The `CERT_EXPIRY_30D` alert announces it. The certificates cover 12 hostnames.

## Before you start

- Have the change record open.
- Confirm no deploy is running in #deploys.
- Check that the internal CA is healthy.

## Rotation steps

!! Never delete the old private key before step 6. Rollback depends on it.

1. Confirm expiry
-- 1. Run `openssl x509 -enddate -noout` on the live certificate.
-- 2. Compare the date with the alert.
2. Request the new certificate
-- 1. Run `certctl request --profile edge-prod`.
-- 2. Check that the output lists all 12 hostnames.
3. Stage it on the canary proxy `edge-canary-01` only
-- 1. Copy it to `/etc/edge/certs/next`.
-- 2. Reload the proxy.
4. Verify the canary
-- 1. `openssl s_client -connect edge-canary-01:443` shows the new expiry date.
-- 2. Handshake errors stay under 0.1% for 20 minutes.
5. Roll out to the other 17 proxies in batches of 3, waiting 5 minutes between batches.
6. Revoke the old certificate after 48 hours and record it in the change record.

## Rollback

The previous certificate stays in `/etc/edge/certs/previous` for 7 days. Copy it back and reload the proxy.

## Escalation

!! Page Platform Security if any proxy shows more than 2% handshake errors.

Then post in #platform-sec.
